Z||000027||onfire||07-02-2001||03:59 AM||||Confusion has strickin'.<P>Well, Saturday her and I were surrounded by a bunch of people, and kids. So we didn't really have much time for ourselves. Plus around 9p.m. her and an old girlfriend that she hadn't seen in 3 years decided to go out and catch up on old times. So I had to wait till today to spend some time alone with her. She had to work so I didn't get over to her house til about 9:15p.m. But I did bring flowers, and she can't remember the last time anyone has ever done that. We talked and listened to music before I had to go. She has to work tomorrow. So the confusion is during our conversation. 90% of the conversation is normal date talk. Then it gradually strays toward relationships, and not being ready for another serious one. I'm like o.k. I can deal with that. I am a patient person. Then she goes on about dating other guys. I'm like o.k. I can deal with that. 99% of the guys out their are jerks, and only want to use women for sex. So I am not worried (sorry lou_dias but I am looking for a serious relationship, sex is secondary don't get me wrong I like sex just as much as the next guy). Besides I am a patient person. Now the confusion starts when she starts saying things like, I like spending time with you. I like talking with you. I'm glad you came over.  Of course all the while we are in each others arms. So on one had she's not ready for a serious relationship to the point of dating other guys. And on the other hand she really, really, really, likes me. Maybe I am reading into things to much. Aaahh what to do?<P>Confusion has stricken.||||reg||1
